com,"$While Johnny Evers was batting, a ball that had been hit"
com,"into the stands was returned to Orval Overall, who was"
com,"coaching at 1B; Overall put the ball in his pocket so as"
com,"not to interupt play; when Evers beat the throw to 1B,"
com,"Overall rolled his ball to umpire Bill Klem, who was"
com,"positioned in the center of the diamond; Evers thought"
com,"it was the ball in play and ran towards 2B; Otto Knabe"
com,"ran to retrieve that ball but the ball in play was still"
com,"held by Kitty Bransfield, who tagged Evers; Klem allowed"
com,"the out even though there were two balls on the field,"
com,"saying that a Cub threw the extra ball onto the field"
